The '''Secretariat of Finance and Civil Service (SFSP)''' is the [[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|secretariat]] of the [[Politics of Balisca|Government of Balisca]] responsible for planning and carrying out the government policy on {{W|public finance}} and [[Confederal budget of Balisca|budget]]. It applies and manages the [[Regions of Balisca|regional]] and local financing systems and the provision of information on the economic-financial activity of the different [[Public Administration of Balisca|Public Administrations]].

The Finance Ministry also manages the {{W|cadastre}} and [[w:Tax collector|collects]] all the confederal [[Taxation in Balisca|taxes]] through the [[Agencia Tributaria]] as well as controlling the {{W|state-owned enterprise}}s through the [[Sociedad Estatal de Participaciones Industriales|State Company of Industrial Participations]] (SEPI). Likewise, the SFSP manages the central government goods, and the [[Loterías y Apuestas del Estado|public lottery]]. However, most of its duties are carried out by autonomous agencies like the [[Balisca Tax Agency|Tax Agency]] and the [[National Mint (Balisca)|National Mint]].

The Secretary is assisted by three main officials, the Secretary of State for Finance, the Secretary of State for Budgets and Expenditures and the Under-Secretary of the Department. This position is analogous to the {{W|finance ministers}} of other nations.

Since 5 January 2025, the current Secretary of the Treasury is [[Elyanna Morejón]].

